WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:08.554
A powerful violent tornado approaches and destroys everything in its path. 

00:00:08.554 --> 00:00:15.204
Your house is now just a pile of rubble. You’ll need to spend many months sheltering elsewhere while your home is rebuilt. 

00:00:15.204 --> 00:00:18.677
Imagine if your home could be rebuilt in days.

00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:27.489
3D printing has the potential to build your house from the ground up faster and for less money than a conventional home

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:33.030
which means amongst other things, no more smoothing concrete by hand.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:38.790
The technology can physically produce a product of almost any shape based on a digital image.

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:45.000
It works by overlapping thin layers of a material, not unlike icing a cake with a piping bag.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.078
And with it,  you can build almost anything your mind can imagine, from children's toys, to prosthetics, to automotive parts.

00:00:52.078 --> 00:00:57.560
The same technology now has the potential to disrupt the entire construction industry.

00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:04.160
Europe’s largest 3D printed residence is currently under construction in the German state of Bavaria.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:10.172
A three-story, 380 square meter, 4,000 square foot apartment complex made of concrete.

00:01:10.172 --> 00:01:17.865
While it normally takes five people five days to build the ground floor, it took two people just one day to do the work with 3D.

00:01:17.865 --> 00:01:20.204
Saving time and cutting costs.

00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:26.046
Further reductions are found in minimizing waste because the printer knows exactly how much material to use

00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:32.591
whereas today, most walls in a house have the same thickness regardless of whether it’s structurally needed or not.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:35.553
This is not the first build of its kind

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:41.439
In 2018, the Ramdanis became the first family ever to move into a 3D printed home 

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:45.959
as part of a social housing project in the northwestern French city of Nantes.

00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:52.445
This house took only 54 hours to print and cost 20% less than a comparable home built the traditional way.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:56.513
White insulator material is layered on both sides of concrete.

00:01:56.513 --> 00:02:01.826
The curved walls that come with more freedom in design improve air circulation and reduce humidity.

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:05.616
In the United States, ICON envisions similar savings.

00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:12.549
The Texas-based company has partnered with a non-profit to build homes for the homeless in Austin and affordable housing in Mexico.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:18.571
Using the latest technology, it can print a 400-500 square foot house in just 24 hours.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:25.601
After building two dozen of the small 3D houses, ICON  is now building much larger homes for the going market rate.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:29.988
But its most ambitious project is out of this world.

00:02:29.988 --> 00:02:38.693
NASA has given ICON funding to research and develop a technique for constructing living quarters on the moon by using raw materials.

00:02:38.693 --> 00:02:44.941
The company is experimenting with a substance resembling lunar regolith, the debris that covers the moon’s surface.

00:02:44.941 --> 00:02:50.054
Building in such an environment will take some ingenuity. This is how it could be done.

00:02:50.054 --> 00:02:56.479
The dome of the habitation capsule is inflated and acts as a support structure - just like scaffolding here on Earth.

00:02:56.479 --> 00:03:05.165
Robots scoop up the regolith, then print a shell that’s light, yet strong enough to protect against radiation, meteorites, and temperature fluctuations. 

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:12.591
The same template could be used for Martian habitats which would also rely on natural materials found there.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:21.592
AI Spacefactory plans to create egg-shaped homes based on this prototype called MARSHA, which won NASA’s space habitat competition in 2019.

00:03:21.592 --> 00:03:28.361
The company says MARSHA could be built using basalt fiber extracted from Martian rocks and renewable bioplastic 

00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:36.141
processed from plants grown on the red planet. According to the firm, the material has been tested to be stronger and more durable than concrete.

00:03:36.141 --> 00:03:44.389
Building on Mars is still a long way off of course. But, a similar dwelling is already available for rent closer to home, in upstate New York. 

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:48.609
There are plans to recycle it and re-create more advanced versions across the globe.

00:03:48.609 --> 00:03:53.021
Although 3D printing is spreading, there are still limitations to overcome.

00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:57.260
Some printers don’t work well when temperatures drop below freezing.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.814
Errors in the digital model could result in major issues on site.

00:04:00.814 --> 00:04:03.979
Certain materials, including wood, can’t be printed.

00:04:03.979 --> 00:04:06.995
And printers can’t do all the work...yet.

00:04:06.995 --> 00:04:10.441
Construction workers are still needed to add things like a roof

00:04:10.441 --> 00:04:16.575
but overall the new technologies being used on building sites in the future will require a lot less manual labor.

00:04:16.575 --> 00:04:22.438
A robot recently did all the brickwork for a three-bedroom house under construction in northern England.

00:04:22.438 --> 00:04:28.894
It's not all bad news for the workforce, however, as new, higher-skilled jobs such as modeling can be created.

00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:37.347
One California company, Mighty Buildings, compares the 3D construction industry revolution to the current transformation underway in the auto industry

00:04:37.347 --> 00:04:40.380
with Tesla leading the way with its advanced technology.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:48.373
Mighty Building’s printed studios start at $183,000 in a state where the median home price is $700,000.

00:04:48.373 --> 00:04:57.426
They’re produced in the company’s Oakland factory using a light stone material that hardens when exposed to UV light and is more thermally resistant than concrete.

00:04:57.426 --> 00:05:04.392
Once fully completed, they’re delivered to the site, and plopped down on an existing backyard or soon, on top of a garage.

00:05:04.392 --> 00:05:08.441
The company also has plans to roll out single family homes in the near future.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:17.703
And, as the technology improves, so does the ability to print much larger buildings, like this two-story, 7,000 square foot administrative office in Dubai -

00:05:17.703 --> 00:05:20.319
the largest 3D printed building in the world.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:29.462
The Middle Eastern city is fast becoming an international printing hub and expects to have a quarter of all new buildings 3D printed by 2030.

00:05:30.607 --> 00:05:38.267
It's hard to imagine that rows and rows of pretty much identical houses typical in North American suburbs may no longer be the norm in the future.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:43.493
The construction industry has traditionally been slow when it comes to embracing new technology.

00:05:43.493 --> 00:05:48.588
But 3D printing may prove hard to resist and could quickly become mainstream, 

00:05:48.588 --> 00:05:52.692
providing more and better housing options for people in this world 

00:05:52.692 --> 00:05:54.036
and beyond. 

00:05:54.036 --> 00:05:57.940
The big question is: would you want to live in a 3D printed home? 

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.870
I'm Cindy Pom. Thanks so much for watching.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:03.380
If you like what you saw, give it a like and don't forget to subscribe to my channel.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.029
And thank you very much to my Patrons for your support. 

00:06:06.029 --> 00:06:07.542
I'll see you very soon.

